        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does a Technogym treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 20 October 2026 Technogym’s US store listed the MyRun at $5,390, the Technogym Run at $14,350, the Excite+ Run from $10,460, the Skillmill at $15,250, the Run Personal at $18,640, the Skillrun from $23,090 and the Artis Run from $25,490, with delivery and installation included. Prices change and have risen since 2024.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where are Technogym treadmills made?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Technogym is an Italian company founded in 1983 by Nerio Alessandri and based in Cesena, where its Technogym Village headquarters opened in 2012. It sells in the US through Technogym USA Corp., based in New Jersey. Technogym does not publish where every model and component is made, so ask if that matters to you.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do you need a subscription for a Technogym treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Every model works without one, and Technogym’s app has a free tier. Technogym Plus, with 1,000+ trainer-led Sessions, was $8.99 a month or $89.99 a year when we checked. Technogym says Plus is included with the Technogym Run, Skillrun, Excite, Personal and Artis lines; MyRun buyers get one extra month.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does a Technogym treadmill have in the US?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Technogym’s US sales conditions give a two-year limited warranty on new equipment for home use, excluding wear parts such as cables, rubber and plastic components. For the Technogym Run, Run Personal and Artis Run it offered Care Plus at $1,200, extending cover to four years with labour, parts and wear items.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Technogym MyRun good for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For moderate running, yes; for tall or fast runners it is tight. Its 56.3 by 19.7-inch surface is shorter than the 60 inches usually suggested for running, it reaches 20 km/h (about 12.4 mph) and 12% incline, and it takes users up to 308.6 lb. It has no built-in screen, so you use a tablet.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you buy a Technogym treadmill on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not new from Technogym, as far as we found. Technogym sells its treadmills through its own US store and showrooms, with delivery and installation included. Amazon listings under the Technogym name were mainly parts, covers and older units, so check what a listing actually is and who will install and service it.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
          <div class="author-card">
            <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <div class="ac-k">Written by</div>
              <div class="ac-n"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></div>
              <p class="ac-b">
                Exercise Physiology &amp; Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS. PhD in Kinesiology
